WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:59.000
A splash of fresh water will reach the depths of your heart. Those mighty blue waves can propel you forward or they can calm and soothe. Coast to Michigan coast. Simply feel the flow in the moment. And let those vast lakes, rivers and streams create everlasting memories. Jump right in and let fresh wash over you in Pure Michigan. Keep it fresh at Michigan.org. Or on our website.
一阵清新的水花将触及你心灵的深处。那些汹涌的蓝色海浪可以推动你前行，也可以抚平你的心情。从密歇根的海岸到海岸。只需在当下感受这份流动。让那些浩瀚的湖泊、河流和溪流创造出永恒的记忆。赶快加入进来，在“纯粹密歇根”感受清新的洗礼吧。请登录 Michigan.org 保持新鲜感。或访问我们的网站。

2
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Today's episode deals with a crime committed against a child that won't be suitable for all listeners. Today, the district of Notting Hill in London's inner west is renowned as one of the city's more affluent areas. But in the late 1940s, it was not a desirable place to live. A number of its buildings had been damaged or completely ravaged during the Blitz, an intensive German bombing campaign during the Second World War that killed more than 40,000 civilians. Many of the larger houses that remained standing were sold to landlords who divided them into multi-occupancy dwellings, with tenants leasing either a room or a single story. Ten Rillington Place in Notting Hill's Ladbrook Grove neighborhood was one such abode.
今天的剧集涉及一桩针对儿童的犯罪，可能并不适合所有听众。如今，伦敦内西区的诺丁山地区以该市较为富裕的社区之一而闻名。但在 20 世纪 40 年代后期，这里并不是一个理想的居住地。在第二次世界大战期间，这里的大量建筑在闪电战（德国针对英国的大规模轰炸行动，导致4万多名平民丧生）中遭到破坏或彻底摧毁。许多幸存的大房子被卖给房东，房东将它们分隔成多人合住的住宅，租客们租下一间房或一层楼。诺丁山拉德布鲁克格罗夫社区的灵顿街 10 号就是这样一处住所。

3
00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:42.000
It was the 10th house in a row of narrow, matching three-story brick residences situated at the end of a cul-de-sac that adjoined a busy thoroughfare named St. Mark's Road. All of the houses had been built during the 1870s and by the late 1940s they had fallen into neglect and disrepair. As they were home to so many residents, the street had a bustling atmosphere, with local children often gathering outside to play during the summer months. The landlord for number 10 lived elsewhere. They had split the house into three flats that each occupied an entire story of the building. It was poorly maintained and had no phone or indoor bathroom facilities.
它是尽头死胡同里一排狭窄、相连的三层砖砌住宅中的第 10 座房子，死胡同毗邻一条名为圣马克路的繁忙大道。所有房屋均建于 19 世纪 70 年代，到 20 世纪 40 年代末，它们已经年久失修。由于这里住着如此多的居民，这条街呈现出熙熙攘攘的景象，当地的孩子们经常在夏日聚在外面玩耍。10号的房东住在别处。他们将房子分成了三套公寓，每套公寓占据建筑的一整层。它维护不善，没有电话或室内浴室设施。

4
00:02:42.000 --> 00:03:34.000
Instead, residents had to use bedpans or a lavatory in the backyard, which adjoined a small communal wash house. In March 1948, the property's ground and middle-floor flats were leased to long-term tenants, but the top floor remained available to rent. Newlyweds, Timothy and Beryl Evans had been living with Timothy's parents and sisters just around the corner on St. Mark's Road. Their living quarters were small and crowded. When Beryl discovered she was pregnant, she and Timothy decided it was time to find a place of their own. They were informed of a house nearby that had a sign in its top-floor window reading, Flat to Let. Its affordability, coupled with its convenient location near their extended family,
相反，居民们不得不使用便盆或后院的厕所，后院毗邻一个小型的公共洗衣房。1948 年 3 月，该房产的底层和中间层公寓被长期租户租下，但顶层仍然空置招租。新婚夫妇蒂莫西和贝瑞尔·埃文斯此前一直和蒂莫西的父母及姐妹们住在圣马克路转角处。他们的起居空间既小又拥挤。当贝瑞尔发现自己怀孕时，她和蒂莫西决定是时候找一个属于他们自己的地方了。他们得知附近有一所房子，其顶层窗户上挂着一块写着“出租公寓”的牌子。它负担得起的租金，加上靠近他们大家庭的便利位置，

5
00:03:34.000 --> 00:04:59.000
compelled the Evans' to submit an application, despite the property's less than desirable features. Their submission was approved, and on Monday, March 29, 1948, the young couple moved into 10 Rillington Place. Beryl, Susanna Thorley Beryl Susanna Thorley was born on September 19, 1929, in the south-east London area of Lewisham. She was the oldest of four children, with two younger brothers and a sister. During the Second World War, the Thorleys moved to the west London neighbourhood of Kensington. When Beryl's mother died in 1947, her father relocated to the Seaside Resort of Brighton, roughly 53 miles south of the capital. Beryl remained in London, where she worked as a telephone switchboard operator at Groverner House Hotel on Park Lane, a hotel in the upmarket district of Mayfair.
促使埃文斯夫妇提出了申请，尽管这处房产的条件并非那么理想。他们的申请得到了批准，1948 年 3 月 29 日星期一，这对年轻夫妇搬进了灵顿街 10 号。贝瑞尔·苏珊娜·索利贝瑞尔·苏珊娜·索利于 1929 年 9 月 19 日出生于伦敦东南部刘易舍姆地区。她是四个孩子中的老大，有两个弟弟和一个妹妹。二战期间，索利一家搬到了伦敦西区的肯辛顿。1947年贝瑞尔的母亲去世后，她的父亲搬到了海滨度假胜地布赖顿，该地位于首都以南约 53 英里处。贝瑞尔留在伦敦，在位于梅费尔高档区帕克巷的格罗夫纳豪务酒店担任电话总机接线员。

6
00:04:59.000 --> 00:06:14.000
One of her colleagues was dating a young man, who in turn offered to set Beryl up on a blind date with his friend. Timothy John Evans was born on November 20, 1924, in the Welsh mining town of Murther Tidville, located in the country's south. His father, who worked locally as a coal haulier, abandoned the family seven months before Timothy was born. As a result, Timothy and his older sister Eileen were raised by their mother, Thomasina. In 1929, she remarried another coal worker named Penry Probert. Later that year, the newlyweds had a daughter, Mary. Timothy Evans' childhood was marred by a number of developmental delays. He struggled to walk and speak, though eventually learned how to do both. At age eight, Timothy cut a toe on his right foot on some glass by a river. The wound was bandaged to using a dirty cloth, which led to him developing tubercular veruca, a rash of small, red, papula nodules related to the infectious disease tuberculosis.
她的同事之一当时在和一个年轻男子交往，这名男子转而主动提出让贝瑞尔和他的朋友进行一次相亲。蒂莫西·约翰·埃文斯于 1924 年 11 月 20 日出生于威尔士南部采矿小镇默瑟蒂德维尔。他的父亲是一名当地的煤炭搬运工，在蒂莫西出生前七个月抛弃了家庭。因此，蒂莫西和他的姐姐艾琳是由母亲托马西娜抚养长大的。1929 年，她改嫁给另一位名叫彭里·普罗伯特的煤炭工人。同年晚些时候，这对新婚夫妇生下了一个女儿玛丽。蒂莫西·埃文斯的童年伴随着许多发育迟缓的问题。他在走路和说话方面都很吃力，不过最终学会了这两项技能。八岁时，蒂莫西在河边被玻璃划破了右脚脚趾。伤口用一块脏布包扎，导致他患上了结核性疣，这是一种与结核病相关的、由小型红色丘疹组成的皮疹。

7
00:06:14.000 --> 00:07:33.000
The injury never healed properly, and Timothy was often in hospital receiving treatments. He missed out on much of his schooling, causing his literacy to suffer to the extent that he could barely write and could only read simple texts such as comic books. In 1935, when Timothy was ten years old, the Welsh coalfields were experiencing a depression, so his stepfather relocated to London in search of work. The rest of the family joined him six weeks later, settling in the cities in the West. Timothy continued to miss school due to his ill health. In 1939, he was sent to a clinic in Hampshire that specialized in treating children with tuberculosis and stayed for an entire year. Though the physicians there couldn't entirely fix Timothy's foot injury, they managed to treat it effectively enough that it never bothered him significantly again, though he was left with a permanent limp. By the time he reached adulthood, Timothy stood at five foot five inches tall and had a slight frame. Described as cocky and cheerful, he had dark eyes and dark hair, which he slicked back across his head.
这个伤口一直没有完全愈合，蒂莫西经常在医院接受治疗。他错过了大部分学业，导致他的识字能力受到很大影响，以至于他几乎不会写字，只能阅读漫画书等简单的文本。1935 年，蒂莫西十岁时，威尔士煤田正经历经济萧条，因此他的继父搬到伦敦寻找工作。其余家人六周后也加入了他的行列，定居在伦敦西部。由于身体健康状况不佳，蒂莫西继续逃学。1939 年，他被送到汉普郡的一家诊所，该诊所专门治疗患有结核病的儿童，并在那里待了整整一年。尽管那里的医生无法完全治愈蒂莫西的脚伤，但他们设法将其治疗得足够有效，此后再也没有对他的生活造成严重影响，尽管他留下了一个永久的跛足。到成年时，蒂莫西身高五英尺五英寸，身材瘦弱。他被形容为自负且开朗，拥有一双黑眼睛和向后梳理的黑发。

8
00:07:33.000 --> 00:08:46.000
His leg impairment excused him from military service during World War II, and he remained in London with his family as the city endured the blitz. Although his limited education hindered his work prospects, he managed to secure a job as a car cleaner. Amongst friends and family, Timothy was renowned for exaggerating and telling tall tales. He'd developed the habit as a form of entertainment when he was bedridden as a child. He claimed that his father was an Italian count and that he had a brother who owned an enormous fleet of cars. Though he had a Welsh accent, he would sometimes feign a cockney manner of speaking to fit in with his English friends. Thomasina attributed her son's fibbing to his lack of self-confidence. If caught out in a lie, Timothy would become ashamed and would plead with his mother not to tell his older sister Eileen, whom he adored. In January 1947, shortly after Timothy's 22nd birthday, a friend offered to set him up on a date with a girl named Beryl Thorley.
他的腿部残疾使他在第二次世界大战期间免于服兵役，随着这座城市经受闪电战的摧残，他与家人留在了伦敦。尽管有限的教育阻碍了他的工作前景，但他还是设法找到了一份汽车清洗工的工作。在朋友和家人中，蒂莫西以夸大其词和讲离奇的故事而闻名。他在童年卧病在床时养成了这种习惯，以此作为一种娱乐方式。他声称他的父亲是一位意大利伯爵，并且他有一个拥有一支庞大车队的兄弟。虽然他带有威尔士口音，但他有时会假装伦敦腔的说话方式，以便融入他的英国朋友中。托马西娜将她儿子的编造归咎于他缺乏自信。如果谎言被戳穿，蒂莫西会感到羞耻，并会恳求母亲不要告诉他所崇拜的姐姐艾琳。1947 年 1 月，就在蒂莫西 22 岁生日后不久，一位朋友提出安排他和一位名叫贝瑞尔·索利的女孩约会。

9
00:08:46.000 --> 00:09:52.000
Timothy was drawn to the petite, dark-haired Beryl, and the pair hit it off instantly. They met several more times to attend local dances and to go to the cinema. Within weeks of their first date, they became engaged. On September 20, one day after Beryl's 18th birthday, they married at Kensington Registry Office. Six months later, the couple moved into 10 Rillington Place in preparation of their growing family. Their flat consisted of a single bedroom with a joint living and kitchen space. Despite the cramped quarters and lack of modern amenities, they liked their new home and decided to stay put even when told of a ground floor flat available elsewhere that had its own garden and lavatory. Number 10 Rillington Place had several communal areas, including the hallway, staircase, and outside rear yard, so the evansers often saw their neighbours throughout the day.
蒂莫西被身材娇小、黑发碧眼的贝瑞尔所吸引，两人一拍即合。他们又多次见面，一起去参加当地的舞会和看电影。在第一次约会几周后，他们订婚了。9 月 20 日，即贝瑞尔 18 岁生日的第二天，他们在肯辛顿登记处结婚。六个月后，为了迎接他们不断壮大的家庭，这对夫妇搬进了灵顿街 10 号。他们的公寓由一间卧室以及一个起居室和厨房共用的空间组成。尽管空间局促且缺乏现代便利设施，但他们还是很喜欢这个新家，甚至在得知别处有一套带花园和厕所的底层公寓空出时，也决定留在这里不搬走。灵顿街 10 号有几个公共区域，包括走廊、楼梯和户外的后院，因此埃文斯夫妇在白天经常能见到他们的邻居。

10
00:09:52.000 --> 00:10:49.000
The ground floor flat was home to another married couple, while the middle residence was occupied by an elderly man. Later that year, Timothy commenced a new job as a delivery driver for a food wholesaler. He managed to drive a van all over London, despite having difficulty reading signs and maps. On Sunday, October 10, 1948, Timothy and Beryl welcomed their firstborn, a girl they named Geraldine. Beryl was an affectionate mother, while Timothy spent hours playing with his daughter. He would bring her home small gifts that he collected throughout his delivery shifts. On Wednesday evenings, Thomasina would babysit her grandchild so that the new parents could go to the cinema together. Yet, their relationship grew increasingly fraught and difficult.
底层公寓住着另一对夫妇，而中间的住所则住着一位老。同年晚些时候，蒂莫西开始了一份新工作，担任一家食品批发商的送货司机。尽管阅读路标和地图有困难，他还是设法开着货车跑遍了整个伦敦。1948 年 10 月 10 日星期日，蒂莫西和贝瑞尔迎来了他们的第一个孩子，一个他们取名为杰拉丁的女孩。贝瑞尔是一位慈爱的母亲，而蒂莫西则花数小时和女儿玩耍。他会把他在送货途中收集的小礼物带回家。每周三晚上，托马西娜都会帮他们照看孙女，这样这对新手父母就可以一起去看电影了。然而，他们的关系变得越来越紧张和困难。

11
00:10:49.000 --> 00:11:42.000
Money was scarce. They struggled to afford rent and make repayments on their furniture. Timothy felt his wife did not know how to cook, clean, or manage a household budget. Beryl was frustrated at the amount of time and money her husband spent drinking at local pubs. He also had a quick temper that was exacerbated by alcohol. Their neighbours overheard their loud arguments, which sometimes became physical. By July 1949, Beryl had returned to work part-time to support her family. She struck up a mild flirtation with a colleague and once teased Timothy about it when he paid her a visit. He slapped her, and the pair caused a scene that resulted in Beryl losing her job.
金钱匮乏。他们很难支付房租和偿还家具分期付款。蒂莫西觉得他的妻子不知道如何做饭、打扫卫生或管理家庭预算。贝瑞尔则对她丈夫花在当地酒馆喝酒的时间和金钱感到沮丧。他脾气暴躁，酒精更是加剧了这一缺点。他们的邻居无意中听到了他们大声的争吵，有时甚至演变成肢体冲突。到 1949 年 7 月，贝瑞尔为了补贴家用，已经重返兼职工作。她与一位同事产生了轻微的暧昧关系，有一次在蒂莫西去看望她时还拿这件事逗他。他打了她一巴掌，两人闹出了乱子，导致贝瑞尔丢了工作。

12
00:11:42.000 --> 00:12:41.000
On another occasion, Beryl threw a jar of baby cream at her husband, causing a gash that required stitches. Beryl's father concluded that his daughter was unhappily married, and her relationship with Timothy was not, quote, a genuine friendship. Other relatives and acquaintances were of the opposite opinion, believing the couple were happy and in love. Timothy's younger sister, Mary, attributed their marital issues to struggling to make ends meet in post-war London. A young girl who babysat Geraldine described them as a lovely couple, very fond of each other. They did quarrel a bit, but never badly, and never for long. On the evening of August 28, 1949, a police officer was called to 10 Rillington Place following reports of a loud fight.
在另一次事件中，贝瑞尔向丈夫扔了一罐婴儿面霜，导致他脸部被割伤，需要缝针。贝瑞尔的父亲得出结论，他的女儿婚姻不幸福，她与蒂莫西的关系“算不上真正的友谊”。其他亲戚和熟人则持相反观点，认为这对夫妇很幸福并且深爱着对方。蒂莫西的妹妹玛丽将他们的婚姻问题归咎于在战后伦敦难以维持生计。一个曾照看过杰拉丁的小女孩形容他们是一对恩爱夫妻，彼此非常喜爱。他们确实会争吵几句，但从不严重，也从不持久。1949 年 8 月 28 日晚上，一名警官接到关于激烈争吵的报警电话，被召至灵顿街 10 号。

13
00:12:41.000 --> 00:13:33.000
In the top floor flat, they found Timothy, Beryl, Tomasina, and a teenage girl in the midst of an argument. The girl, 17-year-old Lucy Endicott, was a friend of Beryl's who was temporarily staying with the Evans''. Beryl had slapped Lucy after accusing her of sleeping with her husband the previous night. Tomasina was demanding Lucy leave as her presence was causing problems in her son's marriage. Lucy denied the allegations. She claimed to have witnessed Timothy beat Beryl and threatened to throw her out of a window. The feud ended with Lucy and Timothy leaving the flat. They stayed together for two nights until Lucy tired of his company and went home to her mother.
在顶层公寓里，他们发现蒂莫西、贝瑞尔、托马西娜和一个十几岁的女孩正处于激烈的争吵中。这个名叫露西·恩迪科特的 17 岁女孩是贝瑞尔的朋友，当时正暂住在埃文斯家。贝瑞尔扇了露西耳光，指控她在前一晚与自己的丈夫发生过性关系。托马西娜则要求露西离开，因为她的存在正在给她儿子的婚姻带来问题。露西否认了这些指控。她声称目睹了蒂莫西殴打贝瑞尔，并威胁要把她扔出窗外。这场争吵以露西和蒂莫西离开公寓而告终。他们在一起呆了两晚，直到露西厌倦了他的陪伴并回家找母亲。

14
00:13:33.000 --> 00:14:40.000
Timothy returned to Beryl, who accepted him back. At around 7am on Tuesday, November 15, 1949, Cornelius Lynch was in the midst of preparing for work when he heard a knock on the front door. He was surprised to greet his 24-year-old nephew, Timothy Evans, the son of his sister, Tomasina. Timothy was far from home. Although he was born and raised in Southern Wales, he currently lived in London, 164 miles from Cornelius's house in the Welsh village of Murthervale. Timothy informed his uncle that he had been travelling with his boss searching for areas to expand his food wholesaler business. Their car broke down in the city of Cardiff, about half an hour's drive south, leaving them stranded for a few days at least. Cornelius and his wife, Violet, were happy to let their nephew stay with them for as long as he needed.
蒂莫西回到了贝瑞尔身边，而贝瑞尔接纳了他。1949 年 11 月 15 日星期二早晨 7 点左右，科尼利厄斯·林奇正准备去上班，突然听到敲门声。他惊喜地迎来了他 24 岁的侄子蒂莫西·埃文斯，也就是他姐姐托马西娜的儿子。蒂莫西离家很远。尽管他在南威尔士出生长大，但他目前住在伦敦，距离科尼利厄斯在威尔士村庄默瑟维尔的家有 164 英里。蒂莫西告诉他的叔叔，他一直在和他的老板一起旅行，寻找扩大其食品批发业务的地区。他们的汽车在卡迪夫市抛锚了，卡迪夫在南面约半小时车程的地方，这使他们至少滞留了几天。科尼利厄斯和他的妻子维奥莱特很高兴让他们的侄子在他们家住多久都行。

15
00:14:40.000 --> 00:15:41.000
Timothy spent the following days going for walks in the nearby hills, reading comics by the fire and accompanying his aunt on shopping errands. A week-long absence from home would go unnoticed, as Beryl was holidaying at her widowed father's place in Brighton and had taken one-year-old Geraldine with her. A framed picture of the infant was displayed in the Lynch's house, and Timothy was often caught talking to it. On one occasion, he turned to his aunt, Violet, and told her, Just wait till you see her, Auntie Violet. She's a smasher. While at a pub with his nephew one day, Cornelius noticed Timothy holding what appeared to be a woman's wedding ring. When asked if it was Beryl's, Timothy said no, he'd just found it somewhere. He also gifted an old friend's wife a necklace, though didn't reveal where it had come from.
接下来的几天里，蒂莫西在附近的山丘上散步，在火炉旁读漫画书，并陪同他的阿姨采购杂货。由于贝瑞尔当时正在布赖顿她丧偶的父亲家度假，并且带上了一岁的杰拉丁，因此他离家一周并未引起注意。林奇家中摆放着一张婴儿的框装照片，蒂莫西经常被发现对着照片自言自语。有一次，他转向他的阿姨维奥莱特，对她说：“等您见到她就知道了，维奥莱特阿姨。她是个标致的孩子。”一天，在和侄子一起去酒馆时，科尼利厄斯注意到蒂莫西手里拿着一件看起来像是女性结婚戒指的东西。当被问及这是否是贝瑞尔的时，蒂莫西说不是，他只是在某个地方捡到的。他还送给了一位老朋友的妻子一条项链，但没有透露它是从哪里来的。

16
00:15:41.000 --> 00:16:44.000
On his fifth day in Murthervale, Timothy celebrated his 25th birthday. He left the following day of Monday, November 21, telling the Lynch's he needed to meet his boss in Cardiff to collect some pay and expenses. Three days later, Timothy reappeared. He admitted to his aunt and uncle that he never went to Cardiff, he had actually been back to London. When asked if he had seen his wife and daughter during his brief trip home, Timothy replied that he had. He revealed that Beryl had walked out on him and baby Geraldine. During his journey back to Murthervale, he dropped his daughter off with some acquaintances in the city of Newport, just outside of Cardiff. The Lynch's were suspicious of their nephew's odd behavior and confusing explanations and were not inclined to believe that Beryl had abandoned him and her baby.
在默瑟维尔的第五天，蒂莫西庆祝了他的 25 岁生日。他在第二天（11 月 21 日星期一）离开，告诉林奇夫妇他需要去卡迪夫见他的老板以领取一些工资和报销费用。三天后，蒂莫西再次出现。他向他的叔叔和阿姨承认，他根本没有去卡迪夫，实际上是回过伦敦。当被问及他在短暂的回家之行中是否见过他的妻子和女儿时，蒂莫西回答说他见过了。他透露说，贝瑞尔抛弃了他和婴儿杰拉丁离家出走了。在返回默瑟维尔的途中，他把女儿留在了卡迪夫郊外纽波特市的一些熟人那里。林奇夫妇对侄子古怪的行为和混乱的解释产生怀疑，并不倾向于相信贝瑞尔抛弃了他和孩子。

17
00:16:44.000 --> 00:17:52.000
One night, Cornelius asked Timothy to again confirm what had happened. He changed his story, this time saying Beryl was pregnant by another man so he had left her and would never see her again. Meanwhile, Timothy's mother and sisters hadn't heard from him in more than a fortnight. On Sunday, November 27, Timothy's sister Eileen visited 10 Rillington Place only to find the Evans' top story flat quiet. She inquired with the neighbors and spoke to the occupants of the ground floor flat, a middle-aged couple named John and Ethel Christie. Ethel reported that Beryl had left the property with Geraldine almost three weeks earlier on Tuesday, November 8. She was certain of it as she helped Beryl carry her bags. Ethel's husband to John told Eileen, they've had a row, best to leave young couples alone.
一天晚上，科尼利厄斯要求蒂莫西再次确认发生了什么事。他改变了说法，这一次他说贝瑞尔怀上了别人的孩子，所以他离开了他，并且再也不会见到她了。与此同时，蒂莫西的母亲和姐妹们已经有两周多没有听到他的消息了。11 月 27 日星期日，蒂莫西的妹妹艾琳拜访了灵顿街 10 号，却发现埃文斯家的顶层公寓静悄悄的。她向邻居打听，并与底层公寓的住户（一对名叫约翰和埃瑟尔·克里斯特的中年夫妇）进行了交谈。埃瑟尔报告说，贝瑞尔在大约三周前的 11 月 8 日星期二带着杰拉丁离开了这里。她对此确信不疑，因为她曾帮贝瑞尔拎过行李。埃瑟尔的丈夫约翰对艾琳说：“他们吵了一架，最好别管年轻夫妇的事。”

18
00:17:52.000 --> 00:19:03.000
The following day, Timothy's other sister Mary arrived at Rillington Place to carry out her own investigations. She also spoke with the Christie's and couldn't understand why Beryl hadn't written as she must have known they would worry if they didn't hear from her. John Christie revealed that Timothy had sold all the couple's furniture as though he had no intention to return. It appeared to have been in response to his mother, who was interfering with the couple's lives too much. John stated that Beryl left without saying goodbye, though his wife claimed otherwise, explaining Beryl bid her farewell and stated she would write. Mary planned to contact the police if she didn't hear from her brother or Beryl by the end of the week. John Christie advised her against it, as Timothy would not thank her if she involved the authorities in his personal matters. When Tomasina last spoke with her son, he claimed that Beryl and Geraldine were holidaying in Brighton.
第二天，蒂莫西的另一个妹妹玛丽来到灵顿街进行她自己的调查。她也与克里斯特夫妇交谈了，不明白为什么贝瑞尔没有写信，因为她一定知道如果听不到她的消息，他们会担心的。约翰·克里斯特透露，蒂莫西卖掉了这对夫妇所有的家具，仿佛他无意回来一样。这似乎是对他母亲干涉这对夫妇生活太多的回应。约翰声称贝瑞尔没有道别就离开了，尽管他的妻子声称并非如此，并解释说贝瑞尔向她告别并表示她会写信。玛丽计划如果到周末还没有听到她哥哥或贝瑞尔的消息就联系警方。约翰·克里斯特劝她不要这么做，因为如果她把当局卷入他的个人事务，蒂莫西是不会感谢她的。托马西娜最后一次与她儿子交谈时，他声称贝瑞尔和杰拉丁正在布赖顿度假。

19
00:19:03.000 --> 00:20:34.000
Yet, it had been almost a month since the otherwise communicative Beryl contacted her in-laws. Tomasina sent a telegram to Beryl's father in Brighton, as she had purchased a dress for Geraldine as a Christmas gift and wanted to confirm Beryl would still be there before sending it. In his reply, Beryl's father revealed that his daughter hadn't been staying with him. A short time later, Tomasina received a letter from her sister-in-law, Violet Lynch, informing her that Timothy had spent the previous two weeks at her home in Murthervale. A number of individuals told Tomasina that her son owed them money, leading her to suspect he had run away from his debts. Furious that Timothy was lying and had seemingly abandoned his responsibilities, Tomasina wrote back to Violet. She panned. There is some mystery about him. You can tell him from me. I never want to see him again as long as I live. He packed up a good job here. He is like his father. No good to himself or anybody else. Violet Lynch received Tomasina's letter the morning of Wednesday, November 30. She read it to Timothy at the breakfast table before accusing him of lying.
然而，距离这位平时爱沟通的贝瑞尔联系她的公公婆婆已经过去近一个月了。托马西娜给布赖顿的贝瑞尔的父亲发了一封电报，因为她为杰拉丁买了一件裙子作为圣诞礼物，想在寄出之前确认贝瑞尔是否还在那里。在回信中，贝瑞尔的父亲透露他的女儿并没有和他住在一起。不久之后，托马西娜收到她的大嫂维奥莱特·林奇的信，告知她蒂莫西在默瑟维尔的家中度过了过去的两周。许多人告诉托马西娜，她的儿子欠他们钱，这导致她怀疑他逃避债务。托马西娜对蒂莫西撒谎并似乎抛弃了责任感到愤怒，于是回信给维奥莱特。她写道：“他身上有些谜团。你可以替我告诉他。只要我活着，我再也不想见到他了。他在这里辞掉了一份好工作。他就像他父亲一样。对自已对别人都没有好处。”维奥莱特·林奇在 11 月 30 日星期三早晨收到了托马西娜的信。她在餐桌上读给蒂莫西听，然后指责他在撒谎。

20
00:20:34.000 --> 00:21:55.000
He maintained his story that Beryl and Geraldine were in Brighton. He also denied selling their furniture. He appeared anxious and didn't finish eating his meal. At 3.10 that afternoon, he walked into Murthervale's police station. Timothy told the officer on duty, Detective Constable Gwynfren Evans, I would like to have a chat with you alone. He was taken into the station's charge office, where he announced, I want to give myself up. I have disposed of my wife. When asked what he meant, Timothy elaborated. I put her down the drain. The detective queried whether Timothy knew what he was admitting to. He answered, Yes, I know what I'm saying. I can't sleep and want to get it off my chest. He was cautioned and asked if he wanted to make a written statement. As he couldn't read or write, Timothy suggested he talk about it while officers dictated. He was then transferred five miles north to the criminal investigation department in his hometown of Murther Tidville.
他坚持他的说法，即贝瑞尔和杰拉丁在布赖顿。他还否认出卖了他们的家具。他显得很焦虑，没有吃完饭。那天下午 3 点 10 分，他走进了默瑟维尔的警察局。蒂莫西对值班警官、侦探警员格温弗伦·埃文斯说：“我想单独和您聊聊。”他被带到警察局的值班室，在那里他宣布：“我要自首。我处理掉了我的妻子。”当被问及这是什么意思时，蒂莫西详细解释道：“我把她扔进下水道了。”侦探询问蒂莫西是否知道自己在承认什么。他回答说：“是的，我知道我在说什么。我睡不着觉，想把它卸载心里。”他受到警告，并被问及是否想发表书面声明。由于他不会读写，蒂莫西建议他在警察口述时谈论此事。随后，他被向北转移了五英里，来到他家乡默瑟蒂德维尔的刑事调查部。

21
00:21:55.000 --> 00:22:57.000
Once there, Timothy gave an official statement to Detective Constable Gwynfren Evans and another officer, Detective Sergeant Glindor Goff. He started with the discovery months earlier that Beryl was pregnant with their second child. The news distressed 19-year-old Beryl, who was already struggling to make ends meet with one child. She had also started a new job at a news agency and would have to quit if she had another baby. She wanted to terminate the pregnancy, but abortions were illegal in the United Kingdom at the time. Timothy didn't share his wife's concern, telling her, If you are having a baby, well, you've had one. Another one won't make any difference. Beryl said about trying to abort the pregnancy herself. Timothy warned that she would only end up making herself unwell, but Beryl was adamant.
到了那里，蒂莫西向侦探警员格温弗伦·埃文斯和另一名警官、侦探警长格林多·高夫作了正式声明。他从几个月前发现贝瑞尔怀上他们的第二个孩子开始讲起。这个消息让 19 岁的贝瑞尔感到苦恼，她带着一个孩子已经很难维持生计了。她还在一家新闻社找到了一份新工作，如果再生一个孩子就不得不辞职。她想终止妊娠，但在当时的英国堕胎是违法的。蒂莫西并不赞同他妻子的担忧，对她说：“如果你要生孩子，好吧，你已经生过一个了。再多一个也没有什么区别。”贝瑞尔谈到要自己尝试流产。蒂莫西警告说，她只会让自己生病，但贝瑞尔态度坚决。

22
00:22:57.000 --> 00:24:15.000
Timothy approached his mother to see whether she knew of anything that could induce a miscarriage. As a practicing Catholic, Tomasina was firmly against the idea. Beryl also discussed the matter with Timothy's sisters, her brother, a friend, and her neighbors, John and Dethyl Christie. At the advice of those she spoke to, she obtained some over-the-counter pills and a syringe to inject glycerine and carboleic soap into her body, but her attempts failed. As time went on, the combination of her unhappy marriage, unwanted pregnancy, and other home remedies caused Beryl to become increasingly ill and emotionally distraught. She confided to her neighbor, Ethyl Christie, that she wanted to have an illegal abortion performed, but couldn't afford one. Then, in early November, Beryl's overall well-being appeared to improve. On Friday, November 4, her brother, Basil, noted that she seemed to be in good spirits, with upcoming plans to go on a holiday with baby Geraldine.
蒂莫西找到他的母亲，看她是否知道有什么东西可以诱发流产。作为一名虔诚的天主教徒，托马西娜坚决反对这个想法。贝瑞尔还与蒂莫西的姐妹、她的兄弟、一个朋友以及她的邻居约翰和黛瑟尔·克里斯特讨论了此事。在他们这些谈话对象的建议下，她买了一些非处方药和一个注射器，用于将甘油和石炭酸皂注入体内，但她的尝试失败了。随着时间的推移，不幸福的婚姻、意外怀孕以及其他民间偏方的结合，导致贝瑞尔的病情日益恶重，情绪也陷入崩溃。她向邻居埃瑟尔·克里斯特吐露，她想做非法堕胎，但负担不起。然后，在 11 月上旬，贝瑞尔的整体身体状况似乎有所改善。11 月 4 日星期五，她的兄弟巴西尔指出，她看起来精神很好，并有即将带着婴儿杰拉丁去度假的计划。

23
00:24:15.000 --> 00:25:16.000
Yet, her husband told a different story. On Sunday, November 6, after a month of trying and failing to induce a miscarriage, Beryl told Timothy that if she couldn't have an abortion, then she would take her own life, as well as Geraldine's. The following morning, Timothy visited a cafe for breakfast. A man sitting nearby engaged him in conversation, asking, You were looking pretty worried. Is there anything on your mind? Timothy shared his troubles with the stranger, who in turn gave him a bottle wrapped in brown paper, stating, Tell your wife to take it first thing in the morning before she has any tea, then to lay down on the bed for a couple of hours, and that should do the job. That night, Beryl went to fetch a cigarette from her husband's coat pocket and discovered the bottle.
然而，她的丈夫却讲述了不同的故事。11 月 6 日星期日，在尝试了一个月却未能诱发流产后，贝瑞尔告诉蒂莫西，如果她不能流产，她将结束自己的生命以及杰拉丁的生命。第二天早上，蒂莫西去一家咖啡馆吃早餐。坐在附近的一名男子与他交谈，问他：“你看起来挺担心的。有什么心事吗？”蒂莫西与陌生人分享了他的烦恼，陌生人转而递给他一个用棕色纸包着的瓶子，并说道：“让你妻子在喝任何茶之前一清早就喝下它，然后躺在床上几个小时，这就行了。”那天晚上，贝瑞尔去从丈夫的外套口袋里拿香烟时发现了这个瓶子。

24
00:25:16.000 --> 00:26:10.000
Timothy spoke of his encounter with the stranger at the cafe, but cautioned her not to consume the bottle's contents. He went to work the next day of Tuesday, November 8. Upon returning home in the evening, he noticed the flat was in darkness. Inside, he found Beryl in bed, deceased. Between 1 and 2 am, he dragged Beryl's body downstairs, out the front door, and lowered her head first into a storm drain. He then smoked a cigarette by the living room fire. Timothy claimed he didn't go to work the next day, and instead resigned, telling his employer that he had received a better offer. He visited his mother to tell her Beryl and Geraldine had gone to Brighton.
蒂莫西讲述了他与咖啡馆陌生人的偶遇，但警告她不要饮用瓶子里的东西。第二天（即 11 月 8 日星期二），他去上班了。晚上回家时，他发现公寓一片黑暗。在里面，他发现贝瑞尔在床上已经断气了。凌晨 1 点到 2 点之间，他把贝瑞尔的尸体拖到楼下，带出前门，把她头部朝下放进了一个雨水渠中。然后他在客厅的火炉旁抽了一支烟。蒂莫西声称他第二天没有去上班，而是辞职了，告诉雇主他收到了更好的报价。他去探望母亲，告诉她贝瑞尔和杰拉丁去了布赖顿。

25
00:26:10.000 --> 00:27:15.000
He then arranged to have a second-hand furniture dealer purchase all of his furniture for £40. The dealer couldn't collect the items until Monday, November 14, so Timothy remained in London for the next five days. Afterwards, he caught a train to Wales to visit his aunt and uncle in Murthervale. He told the officers that he had arranged for someone to look after baby Geraldine before departing. Timothy concluded his statement at 5.10 pm, at which point it was read back to him and he signed it. Three officers were dispatched to 10 Rillington Place, where they spotted a storm drain in the street out front, as Timothy described. Even with their combined strength, they were unable to lift its heavy cover. Their efforts drew the attention of ground floor resident John Christie, who emerged from his flat and re-affirmed that Beryl and Geraldine had left some time ago.
然后他安排了一名二手家具商以 40 英镑的价格购买了他所有的家具。家具商直到 11 月 14 日星期一才能收走这些物品，因此蒂莫西在伦敦又呆了五天。之后，他坐火车去威尔士拜访了他在默瑟维尔的叔叔和阿姨。他告诉警官们，他在离开前已经安排好让人照顾婴儿杰拉丁。蒂莫西在下午 5 点 10 分结束了他的声明，随后该声明被读给他听并且他签了字。三名警官被派往灵顿街 10 号，正如蒂莫西所描述的那样，他们在正前方的街道上发现了一个雨水渠。尽管他们合力，却无法举起沉重的井盖。他们的努力引起了底层居民约翰·克里斯特的注意，他从公寓里走出来，再次确认贝瑞尔和杰拉丁不久前已经离开了。

26
00:27:15.000 --> 00:28:16.000
Through the use of levers, the officers were finally able to lift the storm drain lid. They peered inside, only to find it empty. At approximately 9 pm, Detective Constable Gwynfren Evans returned to where Timothy Evans was being held and told him, the drain which you say you put your wife's body down has been examined and there is nothing there. He replied, well, I put it there. When asked who helped him lift the cover, Timothy stated that he had done so entirely by himself. Given its weight, the detective was skeptical and remarked, I don't think that your wife's body has ever been in the drain. Timothy responded, no, I said that to protect a man named Christie.
通过使用杠杆，警官们终于能够撬开雨水渠盖。他们往里面张望，结果发现里面空无一人。大约晚上 9 点，侦探警员格温弗伦·埃文斯回到关押蒂莫西·埃文斯的地点并告诉他：“你声称把妻子尸体扔进去的下水道已经检查过了，里面什么也没有。”他回答说：“好吧，我把它放在那儿了。”当被问及是谁帮他抬起盖子时，蒂莫西声称那是他自己一个人完全做到的。鉴于其重量，侦探持怀疑态度并评论道：“我认为你妻子的尸体根本就没有在下水道里。”蒂莫西回应说：“没有，我那样说是为了保护一个叫克里斯特的人。”

27
00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:59.000
It's not true about the man in the cafe either. I'll tell you the truth now. He then proceeded to give a second statement which the officers transcribed. He admitted to lying about meeting a stranger in a cafe, but maintained the rest of his statement was essentially true. Roughly a week before Beryl had died, Timothy was approached by his downstairs neighbour, John Christie. John, who was aware of Beryl's attempts to terminate her pregnancy, remarked, I'd like to have a chat with you about your wife taking these tablets. I know what she's taking them for, she's trying to get rid of the baby.
关于咖啡馆里那个人的事也不是真的。我现在把真相告诉你。随后，他接着做出了第二份声明，警官们将其记录了下来。他承认关于在咖啡馆遇到陌生人的事是撒谎，但坚称他声明的其余部分基本属实。在贝瑞尔去世前大约一周，蒂莫西被楼下的邻居约翰·克里斯特搭讪。约翰深知贝瑞尔终止妊娠的企图，评论道：“我想和你谈谈你妻子吃这些药的事。我知道她在吃这些药是为了什么，她想摆脱这个孩子。”

28
00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:57.000
If you or your wife had come to me in the first place, I could have done it for you without any risk. John revealed that he had been studying to be a doctor prior to the outbreak of World War One and showed Timothy a medical textbook he owned. Timothy was unable to read it, but it contained diagrams and illustrations of the human anatomy. John said he could perform an abortion, but cautioned there was a one in ten chance Beryl would die. Timothy was disinterested in the offer and went upstairs to his flat. When he entered, Beryl immediately asked whether John Christie had spoken to him about performing an abortion. Timothy said he had, but told Beryl she wasn't to have anything to do with it. As she trusted John, she intended to take him up on his offer.
